$$1, 1, 1, 2, 4, 7, 11, 17, 27, 44, 72$$
which checks with the answer by  Barry Cipra , with
$$
B_{\,n}  = N(n)\quad A_{\,n}  = \sum\limits_{0\, \le \,k\,} {
\binom{n+1-2k}{n-4k}
  } 
$$ 
