{"input_text": "Question: Calculate the integral
$$ \int \limits_{0}^{1} \frac{x^3-x^2}{\ln x} dx $$ 

Answer: Use substitution $x=e^{-u}$, then 
\begin{align}
I
&= \int_0^1\frac{x^3-x^2}{\ln x}dx \\
&= \int_\infty^0\frac{e^{-3u}-e^{-2u}}{-u}(-e^{-u})du \\
&= -\int_0^\infty\frac{e^{-4u}-e^{-3u}}{u}du \\
&= -\int_0^\infty\frac{1}{s+4}-\frac{1}{s+3}ds \\
&= \ln\dfrac{s+3}{s+4}\Big|_0^\infty \\
&= \color{blue}{\ln\dfrac{4}{3}}
\end{align} 
